# What never belongs in a build of this frontend.
#
# `frontend/Dockerfile` copies by name — `public`, `src`, the three config files — so
# nothing in this list would have reached the image anyway. It still matters, for two
# reasons that are about the build rather than the layer:
#
#  * `docker build` ships the whole context to the daemon before it reads a single line
#    of the Dockerfile. `node_modules` and `.next` between them are hundreds of MB, and
#    `.next` is the previous build on this machine: the cache that makes a stage rebuild
#    when nothing in it changed stop doing so.
#  * `.env.local` holds this project's live values. The Dockerfile never reads it, but a
#    context is a copy of a directory, and there is no reason to hand a copy of a secrets
#    file to a build daemon — or to anyone who can inspect the build cache afterwards.

.git/
.gitignore
.git-scaffold-backup/
**/.git-scaffold-backup/
.vercel/
.vercelignore

# Local secrets. The image is built from `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` build arguments and gets nothing
# else; a browser bundle has no private values in it, which is exactly why `NEXT_PUBLIC_`
# may never be used for one.
.env
.env.*

# Dependencies and build output, re-created inside the image.
node_modules/
.next/
out/
build/
coverage/
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Things that are nobody's business inside an image.
*.log
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db.bak
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
